                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[list][*][b][h1]Morlan's shorts:[/h1][/b][/list]\nIn the pictures it looks good..alas it isn't..\nThis game seems more like a test-bed, an effort in creating a game rather than an actual game. There are many bugs-problems with it. Invisible walls, wrong paths that will lead to dead-end where the only way to leave is..erm.. to die (probably why they call it a dead-end! ) and restart from last checkpoint, which you don't choose but the game decides for you. There's plenty of running, then trying to kill baddies with a crossbow with a very dodgy hitbox that isn't even constant when changing visual settings. Yep, another problem-bug: if you lower some settings, like effects, the torch is flashing instead of having a low-res flame or something, making the game impossible to play for more than a few minutes.\nIt's just a mess.. I reached the level out of the cave and trying at random to see what angle actually works to be able to shoot them baddies. Dying isn't part of the game, it's part of the programming..\nAt least I didn't pay for it, I won it. I don't count that as a win..",
